1. Make sure every file is in your current directory

FOR PURE TERMINAL
2. Type "g++ main.cpp Queue.cpp Stack.cpp -o program.exe" in terminal, this will create a new program.exe file
3. Type "./program" in your terminal. It will run

FOR WEB VERSION (Basic)
2. Type "g++ -std=c++11 -pthread Server1.cpp Queue.cpp Stack.cpp -o server1 -lws2_32 -lwsock32" in terminal, this will create a new server1.exe file
3. Type "./server1" in your terminal
4. Click or CTRL-Click on the website address that is shown or go to "http://localhost:8080/" in your browser

FOR WEB VERSION (Advanced)
2. Type "g++ -std=c++11 -pthread Server2.cpp Queue.cpp Stack.cpp -o server2 -lws2_32 -lwsock32" in terminal, this will create a new server2.exe file
3. Type "./server2" in your terminal
4. Click or CTRL-Click on the website address that is shown or go to "http://localhost:8080/" in your browser
